\tag{fdip}
\title{The graded index}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{At trivial links the centered operator has the zero modes of
\ref{fdip-009Q}. In positive even dimension the volume element
#{C} of \ref{fdip-009X} preserves their space. Its two eigenspaces
separate the zero modes by chirality. When an operator
anticommutes with a grading, how many zero modes of each chirality
can it have? What can change with the connection?}

\p{The dimension question makes sense over a field, on a complex
Hilbert space with an adjoint, and within each irreducible type
of a finite symmetry group.}
